<title>GERMANY: BASF sells unit to Potash Corp. of Saskatechewan.</title>
<headline>BASF sells unit to Potash Corp. of Saskatechewan.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT, Germany</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars figures are U.S.)</p>
<p>German chemicals group BASF AG said Monday its Guano-Werke GmbH subsidiary has sold a 51 percent stake in Kali und Salz Beteiligungs AG to Potash Corp. of Saskatechewan for 250 million marks ($161.4 million).</p>
<p>BASF still holds 25.4 percent of Kali und Salz, a German potash mine owner and operator.</p>
<p>PCS, a leading producer of fertilisers, has an option to purchase the remaining stake at any time before Jan. 1, 2000, for 124.8 million marks ($80.6 million).</p>
</text>
